---
import SiteLayout from "../../../layouts/SiteLayout.astro";
import ThreeDPlayground from "../../../components/ThreeDPlayground.astro";
const base = import.meta.env.BASE_URL;
---
<SiteLayout title="3D Playground — opt-in WebGL" description="A lightweight opt-in WebGL materials and lighting demo. No GPU until requested, with a static SVG fallback and keyboard-friendly controls.">
  <div class="shell page-pad">
    <nav class="breadcrumb" aria-label="Breadcrumb"><a href={base}>Lab home</a><span aria-hidden="true">/</span> 3D Playground</nav>
    <header class="inner-hero">
      <p class="eyebrow"><span class="status-led" aria-hidden="true"></span> LAB 003 / OPTIONAL GPU EXPERIMENT</p>
      <h1>3D Playground<span class="heading-accent">.</span></h1>
      <p>Explore light, material and camera distance on a tiny original cube. You control when the browser allocates graphics resources.</p>
    </header>
    <ThreeDPlayground />
    <section class="below-studio" aria-labelledby="three-d-explained">
      <div><p class="eyebrow">BEHIND THE SCENE</p><h2 id="three-d-explained">One cube, no heavy runtime.</h2></div>
      <div>
        <p>The demonstration draws six original faces with a tiny vertex/fragment shader. All choices are bounded, deterministic and accessible through native inputs; JavaScript and graphics context are only activated after your explicit opt-in.</p>
        <p>Leaving the page releases the buffer and shaders. Motion is manually started and stops on tab hide, offscreen visibility, reduced-motion preference changes or lost GPU context.</p>
        <p><a class="text-link" href="https://github.com/ruslanudintsev-ai/ruslan-ai-lab/issues/8" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">Inspect the 3D test contract ↗</a></p>
      </div>
    </section>
  </div>
</SiteLayout>
